# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING `build/` HERE. build/ is NOT a pure artifact
# directory. Two of its subdirectories are load-bearing and MUST be committed:
#
#   build/rendered/   RUNTIME DATA. The sibling addon questmarks-ui reads these
#                     files off disk and draws each quest's and mission's
#                     description. Ignore them and every description in that
#                     UI disappears.
#   build/authored/   SOURCE OF TRUTH for every step ladder. This is what a
#                     contributor edits to fix a wrong marker; data/*.lua is
#                     downstream of it and is regenerated from it.
#
# Only the three regenerable stages below are ignored. See the README's
# Contributing section for the chain that reproduces them.


# ---- machine-local junk ------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.stackdump
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/

# questmarks writes this on every command; it is a bug-report artifact.
questmarks.log

# One-off probe capture. Nothing reads it.
probe.jsonl

# PER-PLAYER SAVED SETTINGS. Windower writes this on first run; the copy on a
# developer's disk carries real character names and their learned fame levels,
# and its <global> block holds locally-tuned values that would OVERRIDE the
# code defaults in questmarks.lua for anyone who cloned it. Never publish it.
data/settings.xml


# ---- the BG Wiki page cache -------------------------------------------
# ~293 MB of cached wiki HTML across ~3414 pages. It is the audit trail behind
# the CC BY-NC-SA attribution and the input to the page-READING pipeline, but
# it is far too large to publish and neither a player nor a contributor fixing
# a marker needs it. Regenerate with tools/pipeline/fetch_wiki.py -- polite,
# cached and resumable.
bgwiki-rest-cache/pages/
bgwiki-rest-cache/directories/
#
# The rest of bgwiki-rest-cache/ IS committed, deliberately:
#   manifest*.json   the eight run manifests. They carry page ids, revision ids
#                    and per-page content hashes WITHOUT the HTML -- which is
#                    the part the attribution actually needs. ~9.6 MB.
#   supplemental/    a BUILD INPUT, not a cache. emit_lua.py reads
#                    mission_numbers.json and pinned_prepass.py reads
#                    gate_guards.json. Ignoring it breaks the build.


# ---- build/: the regenerable stages only -------------------------------
# Each is reproduced from build/authored/ by the chain in the README.
build/validated/
build/preverify/
build/reports/


# ---- questgraph working state ------------------------------------------
# Derived caches, invalidated by their own .stamp files.
tools/questgraph/cache/

# Point-in-time copies taken before each human correction. The corrected
# record itself lives in build/authored/ and IS committed, carrying its own
# `human` block; these are local undo, not history worth publishing.
tools/questgraph/backups/

# The edit ledger. Every row cites a backup above by ABSOLUTE local path, so
# the file means nothing in a clone. The corrections it logs are in
# build/authored/, which is committed.
tools/questgraph/edits.jsonl


# ---- generated by tools/build_index.lua --------------------------------
tools/unmatched.txt
